L144: # Theming
L145: 
L146: 【99†Previous】 【100†Next】
L147: 
L148: Use CSS Variables to customize the look and feel of your application.
L149: 
L150: 【122†Epicenter Local-first, open source apps Special Sponsor†github.com】
L151: 
L152: We use CSS variables for styling. This allows you to easily change the colors of components without having to update class names.
L153: ## 【112†Convention #】
L154: 
L155: We use a simple `background` and `foreground` convention for colors. The `background` variable is used for the background color of the component and the `foreground` variable is used for the text color.
L156: 
L157: The `background` suffix is omitted when the variable is used for the background color of the component.
L158: 
L159: Given the following CSS variables:
L160: 
L161:     `--primary: oklch(0.205 0 0);
L162:     --primary-foreground: oklch(0.985 0 0);`
L163: 
L164: Copy
L165: The `background` color of the following component will be `var(--primary)` and the `foreground` color will be `var(--primary-foreground)`.
L166: 
L167:     `<div class="bg-primary text-primary-foreground">Hello</div>`
L168: 
L169: Copy
